    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "## Running the Library\n\nStart an SLC session, then run the macro-definition cell. After loading the four source tables into SLC, run the example cell below to define `%cro_example`, then invoke `%cro_example;` in a new SLC cell. Defining the example alone does not run analyses.\n\nUse a single study per call. Required character variables include `treatment_arm`, `baseline_ldl_stratum`, `visit_status`, and the categorical source fields; numeric variables include `age_years`, `bmi_kg_m2`, `baseline_ldl_c_mg_dl`, `visit_week`, `ldl_c_mg_dl`, and `ae_sequence`. This library checks keys but does not implement full schema, date, or controlled-terminology validation. Keep output names different from input names, and do not interpret an old output after a failed rerun.\n\nFor baseline categorical results, use `cro_base_sex_pct` and `cro_base_diabetes_pct`: `within_group_pct` uses the randomized arm-by-stratum denominator, including missing categories. The raw PROC FREQ `PERCENT` column is a whole-table percentage, not that denominator. In continuous summaries, `_FREQ_` is the group record count; each variable has its own nonmissing `N`. LDL summaries report observed-case means, not model-adjusted treatment effects.\n\n**Validation status:** execution was attempted, but SLC returned \"There is no active session.\" The macros have not been compiled or behavior-tested in this environment. Before relying on results, independently test duplicate and missing keys, unmatched participants, missing baseline values, missed visits, zero-event groups, repeated events within a participant, and disposition denominator reconciliation.",
      "executionSummary": {},
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "kind": 2,
      "language": "slc.sasLanguage",
      "value": "%macro cro_example;\n    %if not %sysfunc(exist(work.subjects)) or\n        not %sysfunc(exist(work.labs)) or\n        not %sysfunc(exist(work.adverse_events)) or\n        not %sysfunc(exist(work.disposition)) %then %do;\n        %put ERROR: Load the four EZPill source tables into SLC before running this example.;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    %cro_baseline(subjects=work.subjects, out=work.cro_base);\n    %cro_ldl_derive(subjects=work.subjects, labs=work.labs, out=work.cro_ldl);\n    %if &cro_ok=0 %then %return;\n    %cro_ldl_summary(data=work.cro_ldl, out=work.cro_ldl_stats);\n    %cro_ae_incidence(subjects=work.subjects, ae=work.adverse_events, out=work.cro_ae);\n    %cro_disposition(subjects=work.subjects, disposition=work.disposition, out=work.cro_disp);\n    proc print data=work.cro_ldl_stats(obs=12);\n    run;\n    proc print data=work.cro_ae;\n        where row_type='OVERALL';\n    run;\n    proc print data=work.cro_disp;\n    run;\n%mend;",
      "executionSummary": {},
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    }
